      "message": "This still doesn\u0027t quite match what we\u0027d discussed offline.  We need to tell `DrawWriter` that it needs to include barriers every time it issues a draw call, because it may draw internally if buffers run out of space.\n\nWe also have to inject a flush between draws that don\u0027t otherwise have pipeline/state changes when they overlap so that the barrier orders them correctly. This should be detectable by just comparing `draw.fDrawParams.order().paintOrder()` against the order of the previous draw. If they are equal, they don\u0027t overlap so there\u0027s no barrier needed.",
